Z||000010||turbo86se||04-29-2001||05:05 PM||||Sure you can Slick, but chances are it's going to need to be rebuilt. The turbo itself probably won't cost too much, but the rebuild is rather expensive. <P>My turbo86SE is the sweet black Fiero facing RobertVol's sweet white '88GT on his signature pic.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slick781||04-29-2001||07:44 PM||||i can handle a rebuild... if it isnt like rediculously expensive...  what kind of cars should i look for them to be on?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||AkursedX||04-29-2001||08:31 PM||||Slick 781, yes you can find a turbo in a boneyard and have it rebuilt.  But then you have to do all the plumbing for it, along with configuring the rest of your system to get good use out of it.  What I'm basically saying is that it's alot of work to build a custom turbo system and to get it to run properly.  Personally i think you're best bet would be to look into the Miller-Woods system, or the DesignOne System.  These kits have everything you need and it makes it alot easier to do.  And even with these kits, there is still alot of fine tuning.  There is a guy on the forum only pushing 165hp out of his turbo system because he still needs more tuning done.  I suggest doing a search on the forum about turbos, there is a TON of info on them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
